1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:16,479
All five stories from lessons 1–5 — four pictures each and a full model story in the past tense. Plus twelve phrases that work for any story and five mistakes that cost people points. Get ready and tell the stories out loud!

2
00:00:17,367 --> 00:00:28,321
How does task 3 work? You get four pictures that together tell one story. You tell what happened — in the past tense. You can get ten points for this task.

3
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:52,919
The most important thing is the past tense. Man: šel, měl, byl. Woman: šla, měla, byla. Several people: šli, měli, byli. And when you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem: šel jsem, šla jsem. Now we go through all five stories. First tell it yourself, then you hear the model.

4
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:56,315
Story 1: Moving house.

5
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:58,625
What did the Novák family do yesterday?

6
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:14,131
Yesterday the Novák family moved to a new flat.

7
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,367
In the morning they packed everything into boxes.

8
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:19,300
Mum packed the dishes and the children packed the toys.

9
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,267
Then a big van arrived.

10
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:24,433
Two strong men carried the boxes and furniture to the van.

11
00:01:24,633 --> 00:01:27,100
It was hard, but it went quickly.

12
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,989
In the new flat they put the sofa and the table in place.

13
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,428
Dad put the beds together and Mum cleaned the kitchen.

14
00:01:33,633 --> 00:01:35,600
In the evening everyone was very tired.

15
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,167
They had no time to cook, so they ordered pizza.

16
00:01:38,367 --> 00:01:40,867
They ate it on the floor between the boxes and laughed.

17
00:01:41,067 --> 00:01:43,353
Story 2: A trip to the mountains.

18
00:01:43,667 --> 00:01:45,412
What did Petr and Jana do on Saturday?

19
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,667
On Saturday Petr and Jana went on a trip to the mountains.

20
00:02:00,867 --> 00:02:03,387
In the morning they sat on the train and looked out of the window.

21
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:05,818
It was nice outside and the sun was shining.

22
00:02:06,033 --> 00:02:08,526
Then they walked up the path to the top of the hill.

23
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:11,633
The way was long, but the nature was beautiful.

24
00:02:11,833 --> 00:02:13,433
Suddenly it started to rain.

25
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:17,000
Petr and Jana had no umbrella, so they got completely wet.

26
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,858
Finally they found a small hut.

27
00:02:19,067 --> 00:02:21,267
They sat down at the table and drank hot tea.

28
00:02:21,467 --> 00:02:24,067
They rested and waited for the rain to stop.

29
00:02:24,267 --> 00:02:26,618
Story 3: A bike accident.

30
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:28,885
What happened to Mr Tichý yesterday?

31
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,986
Yesterday morning Mr Tichý was cycling to work.

32
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,767
The weather was nice and he was riding quite fast.

33
00:02:46,967 --> 00:02:49,133
Suddenly a big dog ran onto the road.

34
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:51,867
Mr Tichý wanted to stop but fell off his bike.

35
00:02:52,067 --> 00:02:54,200
His arm hurt and he couldn't get up.

36
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,400
People in the street called an ambulance.

37
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,691
The ambulance came in ten minutes and took him to hospital.

38
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:02,033
At the hospital a doctor examined him.

39
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:04,885
He told him his arm was broken and put it in a cast.

40
00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,392
Mr Tichý had to stay at home for six weeks.

41
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:10,421
Story 4: A lost wallet.

42
00:03:10,733 --> 00:03:12,686
What happened to Mr Dvořák yesterday?

43
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:28,059
Yesterday morning Mr Dvořák took the bus to work.

44
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:30,033
The bus was very crowded.

45
00:03:30,233 --> 00:03:35,022
When he got to work he wanted to buy a coffee, but found that his wallet was gone.

46
00:03:35,233 --> 00:03:40,886
He was nervous because his bank card, driving licence and residence permit were in the wallet.

47
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:43,567
First he called the bank and blocked the card.

48
00:03:43,767 --> 00:03:47,026
In the afternoon he went to the police and reported the lost documents.

49
00:03:47,233 --> 00:03:48,967
The police officer wrote a report.

50
00:03:49,167 --> 00:03:53,494
In the evening the transport company called him: someone had found the wallet on the bus.

51
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:55,549
Story 5: A birthday.

52
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,351
What did Marie do yesterday?

53
00:04:10,067 --> 00:04:11,933
Yesterday it was Marie's birthday.

54
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:15,333
In the morning she got up early and baked a chocolate cake in the kitchen.

55
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:17,617
The cake was big and smelled wonderful.

56
00:04:17,833 --> 00:04:20,131
She put strawberries and whipped cream on the cake.

57
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:21,962
In the afternoon she decorated the flat.

58
00:04:22,167 --> 00:04:24,393
She put colourful balloons in the living room.

59
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,426
Then she prepared food and drinks.

60
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:28,267
In the evening friends came.

61
00:04:28,467 --> 00:04:30,700
They brought Marie presents and flowers.

62
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,433
Marie was very happy.

63
00:04:32,633 --> 00:04:35,700
Then everyone ate cake, sang and danced.

64
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:39,067
The party didn't end until midnight and everyone had a great time.

65
00:04:39,267 --> 00:04:44,809
Now twelve phrases that work for any story. Listen and repeat out loud.

66
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,533
Yesterday morning I got up at seven.

67
00:04:50,733 --> 00:04:52,287
First I had breakfast.

68
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,320
Then I went to work.

69
00:05:00,533 --> 00:05:02,133
Suddenly it started to rain.

70
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:06,860
In the end we went home.

71
00:05:10,067 --> 00:05:12,517
He was tired because he worked a lot.

72
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:18,093
They had no umbrella, so they were wet.

73
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,800
The weather was nice.

74
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,830
In the afternoon she went to the police.

75
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:32,667
Marie had a birthday.

76
00:05:35,867 --> 00:05:37,600
Mr Tichý had to stay at home.

77
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:42,433
In the evening friends came.

78
00:05:45,633 --> 00:05:48,692
Five typical mistakes that cost people points.

79
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:59,536
Correct: Olga ležela v posteli. Tell the story in the past tense: ležela, šla, koupila.

80
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:14,099
Correct: Marie pekla dort. Woman: -la. Man: -l. Several people: -li.

81
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:24,073
Correct: Včera jsem šel do práce. When you talk about yourself, don’t forget jsem.

82
00:06:27,767 --> 00:06:39,581
Correct: Ráno balili věci a potom přijelo auto. Don’t describe the pictures. Tell a story with linking words: nejdřív, potom, nakonec.

83
00:06:43,267 --> 00:06:54,091
Correct: Jel na kole do práce. Najednou vyběhl pes a on spadl. Say two or three sentences for each picture: who, where, what and why.

84
00:06:55,300 --> 00:07:14,873
Summary. First: tell the story in the past tense. Second: link your sentences — nejdřív, potom, nakonec. Third: two or three sentences for each picture. And fourth: watch the gender — on šel, ona šla.

85
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:25,527
Which story is the hardest for you? Write it in the comments — and try to write the first two sentences in the past tense. And if the video helped, give it a like.

86
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:43,341
On the Zkouška A2 nanečisto website you can practise all stories for free — it listens and checks your past tense. Link in the description. Tomorrow: big review of Speaking task 4. Subscribe so you don’t miss anything.
